.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Represents an arbitrary‑precision decimal number stored in scientific notation using a BigInteger mantissa and a base‑10 exponent\&. 

Provides amerikanische (US‑Customary) engineering units directly within \fBBigDecimal\fP\&. These units are widely used in US technical industries, automotive systems, HVAC, construction, and aerospace\&.

.PP
A \fBBigDecimal\fP models values of the form: 
.PP
.nf
value = mantissa × 10^exponent

.fi
.PP
 The mantissa is stored as an unbounded BigInteger, while the exponent is a signed 32‑bit integer\&. This representation allows exact modeling of extremely small or extremely large numbers without rounding artifacts or loss of precision\&. 

.PP
Unlike floating‑point types (\fRfloat\fP, \fRdouble\fP), \fBBigDecimal\fP does not normalize its mantissa automatically\&. The caller may choose any mantissa/exponent combination that represents the desired value\&. This makes the type suitable for scientific, financial, and mathematical applications where deterministic precision and explicit exponent control are required\&. 

.PP
All values are represented exakt as \fBBigDecimal\fP without floating‑ point rounding, making them suitable for precise technical calculations\&. 
